JOURNAL DESKTOP ENTRY POINT

tam-launch-journal [add] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] opens tam-journal in the existing
terminal launcher, under org.tamlinux.journal. The terminal floats on the
focused output. The launcher starts a separate session and returns after exec,
so a calendar helper deadline cannot kill a long journal edit. Arguments
remain argv elements; no shell expression is constructed.

The standalone journal command is supplied by tamlinux-tools. Both must be
included in the selected assembly. An unavailable dependency produces a
failure rather than substituting another notes application.
